Refuse the rollback of a sequence whose recurrent cell other sequences share
Fold-into: upstream/memory

The defects. tests/fuzz/core/run.sh test replays the reproducer of each one.

- A rollback of one sequence moves each sequence that shares its recurrent cell.

  After seq_cp, the source and the destination share one cell of llama_memory_recurrent, with one
  position and one state. A partial seq_rm (a rollback) of one of them sets the position of that
  cell and the rollback index of that sequence only. Thus the other sequence reports the position
  of the rollback (seq_pos_max 2 in place of 3), and its next decode reads a snapshot group with a
  different rollback index. The next decode of a sequence gives it its own cell (find_slot copies
  a shared tail), thus only a rollback between a copy and a decode shows the defect.

  The change: seq_rm refuses the rollback when the tail cell of the sequence holds more than one
  sequence. The caller then decodes the sequence again, as for a rollback deeper than the last
  ubatch. The app does not share cells (n_seq_max = 1).

  The reproducer: tests/fuzz/core/regress/fuzz_recurrent--rollback-shared-cell.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

Files:
